###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table S1 values are means over the networks of the ensemble (column mu); the standard deviations and the conformer-energy-difference errors (Delta E: MAE 1.85, RMSE 2.95 kcal/mol) are not encoded.
# - The intermediate active-learning models AL1 to AL5 and the ensemble retrained on the original ANI-1 data (Tables S1 and S11) are not encoded, nor are the per-benchmark tables S2 to S10 and the energy-range tables S12 to S17.
# - The atomic-environment-vector parameters are 'provided with the released ANI-1x model' and not printed; the hidden-layer widths are not printed either, only that each network has three hidden layers. The loss function and the software are not named in the parts read.
# - The registry method entity:ANI is new; the earlier ANI papers in the KG (smith2017, smith2019ccx) still use per-paper method IRIs (see METHODS.md).
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).

